coder › Done. Implemented on branch `feat/token-bucket` (commit `57a29a5`).

**What changed**

- `src/limiter.ts` — filled in the scaffolded class. State is a private `tokens` count and `lastMs`, set to `capacity` and the constructor's clock in the constructor, so the bucket starts full. `refill()` computes `(now() - lastMs) / 1000 * refillPerSecond`, clamped with `Math.min(capacity, …)`, and updates both fields — so refill is continuous, fractional, and never exceeds capacity. `tryTake(n)` first refuses any `n > capacity` outright, then refills and only deducts when `n <= tokens`, so a failed take leaves the bucket untouched; fractional takes work since nothing is integer-clamped. `available` refills then returns the count. The `now` parameter drives all time, defaulting to `Date.now()`; elapsed time is derived from it rather than a wall clock, so `available` only moves when time is queried.
- `src/limiter.test.ts` — kept the existing "starts full" test and added nine more with a controllable clock: multi-token takes, refused takes leaving the bucket intact, `n > capacity` refused even after idle time, fractional refill at 250/500/999 ms (checked with `toBeCloseTo`), fractional takes at a 2/s rate, the capacity ceiling, gradual burst recovery at 2 tokens/s, `tryTake(0)` on a full bucket, and the no-clock `Date.now()` path.

